s to single into a float-array, as aset rounds it. offset\n  is always a byte offset into p, as in babashka.ffi; a one-byte type fills a\n  byte-array, so (read-into! p :byte arr 0 index count) reads a slice into one.\n  A range outside the array, or an array that cannot hold the type's elements,\n  throws before anything is written." _kc$2952 1358 _kc$2953 1 _kc$2954 "jolt/ffi.clj")))) _kc$2955))) (jolt-register-source! "read-into!" "jolt.ffi" "read-into!" "jolt/ffi.clj" 1358) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1207 "identical?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1266 "count" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1267 "$Rnot" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1267 "number?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1268 "$R+" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1268 "<=" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1269 "ex-info" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1269 "str" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1351 "array-carrier" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1352 "count" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1352 "nil?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1354 "nil?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1355 "$R+" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1355 "__read-into!" #t) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1356 "$R+" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1356 "__read-into-typed!" #t) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1376 "keyword?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1378 "ex-info" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1384 "keyword?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1386 "ex-info" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1386 "str" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1392 "identical?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1393 "$R+" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1393 "__read-into!" #t) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1393 "count" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1393 "nil?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "read-into!" 1395 "ke